# The repository is the game, the rule spec it was written against, the tools that
# measured every number in the README, and the screenshots the README shows.
# What is left below stays on this machine.

# The original pygame program has been deleted from this folder. Its ball sprite is
# the one asset this page never uses — the ball is drawn, not loaded — so it stays
# out of the repo. The kick samples are published: the page uses them when it is
# served over http and synthesises its own kick without them.
ball.png
ball.ico
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Scratch / QA artifacts from this folder: headless-Chrome profiles, captured
# stdout/stderr, temporary DOM dumps, probe frames, split-patch leftovers, logs
.chrome-tmp/
.chrome-*
.check*.png
.o.txt
.e.txt
.a.txt
.b.txt
.ae.txt
.be.txt
.dom.html
.full.txt
.msg
.commitmsg
*.diff
*.patch
*.log

# OS and editor noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# No dependencies today (the tests only need Node itself), but keep this honest
node_modules/
